From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [mp] fix: the connector keeps vLLM's lookahead block hashes
 on, so an MTP prefix hit keeps its last block

vLLM 0.34 resolves its lookahead block hashes (VllmConfig._resolve_num_hash_lookahead_tokens) through the KV connector
class: with EAGLE / MTP it folds the token after each block into the block's hash, which proves the drafter's KV at the
block's last position, only when the connector's supports_lookahead_block_hashes() is True, and the base class returns
False. LMCacheMPConnector did not override it, so with LMCache the engine ran without lookahead hashes and kept the
trailing-block drop: every local prefix-cache hit lost its last matched block, and the align-mode Mamba checkpoints
followed that replay boundary (HybridKVCacheCoordinator sets drop_eagle_checkpoint_block), so a hit whose attention
blocks reached past it fell back to an earlier Mamba state. A hybrid model's alignment makes the block large, and so
the loss per hit; most of LMCache's own hits were the block vLLM had dropped.

The connector now declares the support. Its stores and retrieves follow the request's tokens, never vLLM's block
hashes, and LMCache's chunk keys stay token-only, so spec and non-spec engines keep sharing KV. An LMCache hit that ends
at a chunk boundary may hand the drafter KV computed with another next token, which only the draft acceptance can see:
the target verifies every draft token. This follows LMCache PR #6619 (closed upstream once vLLM main made the support
every connector's default, vLLM PR #65448) and vLLM main's in-tree LMCache connector.

Lazy offload snapshots each block's vLLM hash when a store is offered and drops the store if the hash is missing, and
vLLM hashes a block only once its lookahead tokens exist. With lazy offload, GetStoreMetadata now holds those tokens
back (as #6619 and the open #6699 do), so a chunk-aligned prompt's last chunk is stored once the next token follows.

tests/v1/test_mp_connector_lookahead_opt_in.py resolves vLLM's hash lookahead through the connector class (1 for an
MTP drafter, 0 before this change); tests/v1/test_mp_tracker_store_bound.py covers the held-back chunk; the
hand-built connectors of two tests get the new attribute.
---
